AI image detectors — credits and retained model versions

DDA: Ruoxin Chen, Junwei Xi, Zhiyuan Yan, Keyue Zhang, Shuang Wu, Jingyi Xie, Xu Chen, Lei Xu, Isabel Guan, Taiping Yao and Shouhong Ding. Dual Data Alignment Makes AI-Generated Image Detector Easier Generalizable. Source: https://github.com/roy-ch/Dual-Data-Alignment . Released weights: https://huggingface.co/Junwei-Xi/Dual-Data-Alignment . See the accompanying Apache-2.0 and DINOv2 notices.

PRL: the authors and copyright holders of Relative Patch Response Learning for Generalizable AI-Generated Image Detection. Source: https://github.com/wittyuu/Relative-Patch-Response-Learning . The complete DINOv3 License accompanies its retained backbone; it is not relicensed by this adaptation.

Community Forensics 384: Jeongsoo Park and Andrew Owens. Community Forensics: Using Thousands of Generators to Train Fake Image Detectors, CVPR2025. Source: https://github.com/JeongsooP/Community-Forensics . Weights: https://huggingface.co/OwensLab/commfor-model-384 . Its MIT notice is included.

GAPL: Ziheng Qin, Yuheng Ji, Renshuai Tao, Yuxuan Tian, Yuyang Liu, Yipu Wang and Xiaolong Zheng. Scaling Up AI-Generated Image Detection via Generator-Aware Prototypes. Source: https://github.com/UltraCapture/GAPL . Weights: https://huggingface.co/AbyssLumine/GAPL . The upstream model card and license declaration are included.

Image preparation follows the retained upstream transformations. Pillow resampling attribution and its complete license are included. Runtime dependency notices already accompany the shared ONNX Runtime resources.

The distributed graph payloads are the retained optimized D versions, identified by their unchanged method manifests. Scientific activations/computation are FP32; dense-weight storage includes the declared selective FP16 and INT8 forms. Scores are uncalibrated model indices. Historical conversion inventories are not presented as current D stage identities.
